{"page":36,"verses":[{"verse_key":"2:225","surah":2,"ayah":225,"ar_uthmani":"لَّا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِٱللَّغْوِ فِىٓ أَيْمَـٰنِكُمْ وَلَـٰكِن يُؤَاخِذُكُم بِمَا كَسَبَتْ قُلُوبُكُمْ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"He will not call you to account for oaths you have uttered unintentionally, but He will call you to account for what you mean in your hearts. God is most forgiving and forbearing.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"لَّا","en_gloss":"Not","transliteration":"lā","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":2,"ar":"يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ","en_gloss":"will take you to task","transliteration":"yuākhidhukumu","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":4,"ar":"بِٱللَّغْوِ","en_gloss":"for (what is) unintentional","transliteration":"bil-laghwi","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":5,"ar":"فِىٓ","en_gloss":"in","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":6,"ar":"أَيْمَـٰنِكُمْ","en_gloss":"your oaths","transliteration":"aymānikum","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":7,"ar":"وَلَـٰكِن","en_gloss":"[and] but","transliteration":"walākin","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":8,"ar":"يُؤَاخِذُكُم","en_gloss":"He takes you to task","transliteration":"yuākhidhukum","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":9,"ar":"بِمَا","en_gloss":"for what","transliteration":"bimā","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":10,"ar":"كَسَبَتْ","en_gloss":"(have) earned","transliteration":"kasabat","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":11,"ar":"قُلُوبُكُمْ ۗ","en_gloss":"your hearts","transliteration":"qulūbukum","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":12,"ar":"وَٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"And Allah","transliteration":"wal-lahu","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":13,"ar":"غَفُورٌ","en_gloss":"(is) Oft-Forgiving","transliteration":"ghafūrun","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":14,"ar":"حَلِيمٌۭ","en_gloss":"Most Forbearing","transliteration":"ḥalīmun","verse_key":"2:225"},{"pos":15,"ar":"٢٢٥","en_gloss":"(225)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:225"}]},{"verse_key":"2:226","surah":2,"ayah":226,"ar_uthmani":"لِّلَّذِينَ يُؤْلُونَ مِن نِّسَآئِهِمْ تَرَبُّصُ أَرْبَعَةِ أَشْهُرٍ ۖ فَإِن فَآءُو فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"For those who swear that they will not approach their wives, there shall be a waiting period of four months:if they go back, remember God will be most forgiving and merciful,","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"لِّلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"For those who","transliteration":"lilladhīna","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":2,"ar":"يُؤْلُونَ","en_gloss":"swear (off)","transliteration":"yu'lūna","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مِن","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":4,"ar":"نِّسَآئِهِمْ","en_gloss":"their wives","transliteration":"nisāihim","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":5,"ar":"تَرَبُّصُ","en_gloss":"(is a) waiting (of)","transliteration":"tarabbuṣu","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":6,"ar":"أَرْبَعَةِ","en_gloss":"four","transliteration":"arbaʿati","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":7,"ar":"أَشْهُرٍۢ ۖ","en_gloss":"months","transliteration":"ashhurin","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":8,"ar":"فَإِن","en_gloss":"then if","transliteration":"fa-in","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":9,"ar":"فَآءُو","en_gloss":"they return ","transliteration":"fāū","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":10,"ar":"فَإِنَّ","en_gloss":"then indeed","transliteration":"fa-inna","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":11,"ar":"ٱللَّهَ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-laha","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":12,"ar":"غَفُورٌۭ","en_gloss":"(is) Oft-Forgiving","transliteration":"ghafūrun","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":13,"ar":"رَّحِيمٌۭ","en_gloss":"Most Merciful","transliteration":"raḥīmun","verse_key":"2:226"},{"pos":14,"ar":"٢٢٦","en_gloss":"(226)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:226"}]},{"verse_key":"2:227","surah":2,"ayah":227,"ar_uthmani":"وَإِنْ عَزَمُوا۟ ٱلطَّلَـٰقَ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"but if they are determined to divorce, remember that God hears and knows all.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَإِنْ","en_gloss":"And if","transliteration":"wa-in","verse_key":"2:227"},{"pos":2,"ar":"عَزَمُوا۟","en_gloss":"they resolve","transliteration":"ʿazamū","verse_key":"2:227"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱلطَّلَـٰقَ","en_gloss":"(on) [the] divorce ","transliteration":"l-ṭalāqa","verse_key":"2:227"},{"pos":4,"ar":"فَإِنَّ","en_gloss":"then indeed","transliteration":"fa-inna","verse_key":"2:227"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ٱللَّهَ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-laha","verse_key":"2:227"},{"pos":6,"ar":"سَمِيعٌ","en_gloss":"(is) All-Hearing","transliteration":"samīʿun","verse_key":"2:227"},{"pos":7,"ar":"عَلِيمٌۭ","en_gloss":"All-Knowing","transliteration":"ʿalīmun","verse_key":"2:227"},{"pos":8,"ar":"٢٢٧","en_gloss":"(227)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:227"}]},{"verse_key":"2:228","surah":2,"ayah":228,"ar_uthmani":"وَٱلْمُطَلَّقَـٰتُ يَتَرَبَّصْنَ بِأَنفُسِهِنَّ ثَلَـٰثَةَ قُرُوٓءٍ ۚ وَلَا يَحِلُّ لَهُنَّ أَن يَكْتُمْنَ مَا خَلَقَ ٱللَّهُ فِىٓ أَرْحَامِهِنَّ إِن كُنَّ يُؤْمِنَّ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلْيَوْمِ ٱلْـَٔاخِرِ ۚ وَبُعُولَتُهُنَّ أَحَقُّ بِرَدِّهِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ إِنْ أَرَادُوٓا۟ إِصْلَـٰحًا ۚ وَلَهُنَّ مِثْلُ ٱلَّذِى عَلَيْهِنَّ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ ۚ وَلِلرِّجَالِ عَلَيْهِنَّ دَرَجَةٌ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Divorced women must wait for three monthly periods before remarrying, and, if they really believe in God and the Last Day, it is not lawful for them to conceal what God has created in their wombs: their husbands would do better to take them back during this period, provided they wish to put things right. Wives have [rights] similar to their [obligations], according to what is recognized to be fair, and husbands have a degree [of right] over them: [both should remember that] God is almighty and wise.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَٱلْمُطَلَّقَـٰتُ","en_gloss":"And the women who are divorced","transliteration":"wal-muṭalaqātu","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":2,"ar":"يَتَرَبَّصْنَ","en_gloss":"shall wait","transliteration":"yatarabbaṣna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":3,"ar":"بِأَنفُسِهِنَّ","en_gloss":"concerning themselves","transliteration":"bi-anfusihinna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":4,"ar":"ثَلَـٰثَةَ","en_gloss":"(for) three","transliteration":"thalāthata","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":5,"ar":"قُرُوٓءٍۢ ۚ","en_gloss":"monthly periods","transliteration":"qurūin","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":6,"ar":"وَلَا","en_gloss":"And (it is) not","transliteration":"walā","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":7,"ar":"يَحِلُّ","en_gloss":"lawful","transliteration":"yaḥillu","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":8,"ar":"لَهُنَّ","en_gloss":"for them","transliteration":"lahunna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":9,"ar":"أَن","en_gloss":"that","transliteration":"an","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":10,"ar":"يَكْتُمْنَ","en_gloss":"they conceal","transliteration":"yaktum'na","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":11,"ar":"مَا","en_gloss":"what","transliteration":"mā","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":12,"ar":"خَلَقَ","en_gloss":"(has been) created","transliteration":"khalaqa","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":13,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"(by) Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":14,"ar":"فِىٓ","en_gloss":"in","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":15,"ar":"أَرْحَامِهِنَّ","en_gloss":"their wombs","transliteration":"arḥāmihinna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":16,"ar":"إِن","en_gloss":"if","transliteration":"in","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":17,"ar":"كُنَّ","en_gloss":"they","transliteration":"kunna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":18,"ar":"يُؤْمِنَّ","en_gloss":"believe","transliteration":"yu'minna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":19,"ar":"بِٱللَّهِ","en_gloss":"in Allah","transliteration":"bil-lahi","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":20,"ar":"وَٱلْيَوْمِ","en_gloss":"and the Day","transliteration":"wal-yawmi","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":21,"ar":"ٱلْـَٔاخِرِ ۚ","en_gloss":"[the] Last","transliteration":"l-ākhiri","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":22,"ar":"وَبُعُولَتُهُنَّ","en_gloss":"And their husbands","transliteration":"wabuʿūlatuhunna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":23,"ar":"أَحَقُّ","en_gloss":"(have) better right","transliteration":"aḥaqqu","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":24,"ar":"بِرَدِّهِنَّ","en_gloss":"to take them back","transliteration":"biraddihinna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":25,"ar":"فِى","en_gloss":"in","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":26,"ar":"ذَٰلِكَ","en_gloss":"that (period)","transliteration":"dhālika","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":27,"ar":"إِنْ","en_gloss":"if","transliteration":"in","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":28,"ar":"أَرَادُوٓا۟","en_gloss":"they wish","transliteration":"arādū","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":29,"ar":"إِصْلَـٰحًۭا ۚ","en_gloss":"(for) reconciliation","transliteration":"iṣ'lāḥan","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":30,"ar":"وَلَهُنَّ","en_gloss":"And for them","transliteration":"walahunna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":31,"ar":"مِثْلُ","en_gloss":"(is the) like","transliteration":"mith'lu","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":32,"ar":"ٱلَّذِى","en_gloss":"(of) that which","transliteration":"alladhī","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":33,"ar":"عَلَيْهِنَّ","en_gloss":"(is) on them","transliteration":"ʿalayhinna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":34,"ar":"بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ ۚ","en_gloss":"in a reasonable manner","transliteration":"bil-maʿrūfi","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":35,"ar":"وَلِلرِّجَالِ","en_gloss":"and for the men","transliteration":"walilrrijāli","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":36,"ar":"عَلَيْهِنَّ","en_gloss":"over them","transliteration":"ʿalayhinna","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":37,"ar":"دَرَجَةٌۭ ۗ","en_gloss":"(is) a degree","transliteration":"darajatun","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":38,"ar":"وَٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"And Allah","transliteration":"wal-lahu","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":39,"ar":"عَزِيزٌ","en_gloss":"(is) All-Mighty","transliteration":"ʿazīzun","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":40,"ar":"حَكِيمٌ","en_gloss":"All-Wise","transliteration":"ḥakīmun","verse_key":"2:228"},{"pos":41,"ar":"٢٢٨","en_gloss":"(228)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:228"}]},{"verse_key":"2:229","surah":2,"ayah":229,"ar_uthmani":"ٱلطَّلَـٰقُ مَرَّتَانِ ۖ فَإِمْسَاكٌۢ بِمَعْرُوفٍ أَوْ تَسْرِيحٌۢ بِإِحْسَـٰنٍ ۗ وَلَا يَحِلُّ لَكُمْ أَن تَأْخُذُوا۟ مِمَّآ ءَاتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ شَيْـًٔا إِلَّآ أَن يَخَافَآ أَلَّا يُقِيمَا حُدُودَ ٱللَّهِ ۖ فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلَّا يُقِيمَا حُدُودَ ٱللَّهِ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَا فِيمَا ٱفْتَدَتْ بِهِۦ ۗ تِلْكَ حُدُودُ ٱللَّهِ فَلَا تَعْتَدُوهَا ۚ وَمَن يَتَعَدَّ حُدُودَ ٱللَّهِ فَأُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلظَّـٰلِمُونَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Divorce can happen twice, and [each time] wives either be kept on in an acceptable manner or released in a good way. It is not lawful for you to take back anything that you have given [your wives], except where both fear that they cannot maintain [the marriage] within the bounds set by God: if you [arbiters] suspect that the couple may not be able to do this, then there will be no blame on either of them if the woman opts to give something for her release. These are the bounds set by God: do not overstep them. It is those who overstep God’s bounds who are doing wrong.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"ٱلطَّلَـٰقُ","en_gloss":"The divorce","transliteration":"al-ṭalāqu","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":2,"ar":"مَرَّتَانِ ۖ","en_gloss":"(is) twice","transliteration":"marratāni","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":3,"ar":"فَإِمْسَاكٌۢ","en_gloss":"Then to retain","transliteration":"fa-im'sākun","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":4,"ar":"بِمَعْرُوفٍ","en_gloss":"in a reasonable manner","transliteration":"bimaʿrūfin","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":5,"ar":"أَوْ","en_gloss":"or","transliteration":"aw","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":6,"ar":"تَسْرِيحٌۢ","en_gloss":"to release (her)","transliteration":"tasrīḥun","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":7,"ar":"بِإِحْسَـٰنٍۢ ۗ","en_gloss":"with kindness","transliteration":"bi-iḥ'sānin","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":8,"ar":"وَلَا","en_gloss":"And (it is) not","transliteration":"walā","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":9,"ar":"يَحِلُّ","en_gloss":"lawful","transliteration":"yaḥillu","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":10,"ar":"لَكُمْ","en_gloss":"for you","transliteration":"lakum","verse_key":"2:229"},{"pos":11,"a